  "body": "We know that in HTML5 we can use `<del>` and `<ins>` to mark a deleted and an inserted text/HTML content, respectively. For example:\r\n\r\n    This is a text with <del datetime=\"2015-09-15T22:55:03Z\">removed</del><ins datetime=\"2016-09-15T22:55:03Z\">inserted</ins> content.\r\n\r\nWhat is the corresponding way to mark the insertion/deletion of an element? For example, to mark the `<strong>` below as an inserted element and the `<em>` element below as a deleted styling element (and has no styling effect):\r\n\r\n    This is a text with <strong><em>a text content whose styling has been changed</em></strong>.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, what is the way to mark the insertion/deletion of an attribute? For example, to mark the `<span>` element below as having 'class=\"foo\"' added and 'class=\"bar\"' removed:\r\n\r\n    This is <span class=\"foo\">an element whose class has been changed</span>.",
